<body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="site-header"><div class="container header-inner">
<a class="wordmark" href="#main" aria-label="Aberration home"><svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M10 10H38V20H20V54H10ZM44 10H54V54H26V44H44Z"/></svg><span>aberration</span></a>
<span class="header-statement mono">Real-time decision-making.</span>
<nav class="header-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a class="nav-cta" href="{{ frontend_base_url | e }}/">Dashboard <svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
<path d="M7 17 17 7M7 7h10v10"/></svg></a></nav>
</div></header><main id="main">
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="headline">
  <figure class="hero-photo">
    {% for subject, word, file, width, description in hero_slides %}
    <img class="hero-photo--{{ subject }}" src="/assets/{{ file }}" width="{{ width }}" height="809" {% if loop.first %}fetchpriority="high"{% else %}decoding="async"{% endif %} alt="Generated photograph looking along the underside of {{ description }}.">
    {% endfor %}
  </figure>
  <div class="hero-title">
    <p class="mono">Anomaly detection for physical &amp; digital systems</p>
    <h1 id="headline">Every system has a pattern.</h1>
    <p class="hero-promise"><span class="visually-hidden">Detect when strain, traffic, flow, quality, yield, efficiency, precision or pressure changes.</span><span aria-hidden="true"><span class="hero-promise-prefix">Detect when </span><span class="hero-words">{% for subject, word, file, width, description in hero_slides %}<span class="hero-word hero-word--{{ subject }}">{{ word }}</span>{% endfor %}</span><span class="hero-promise-suffix"> changes.</span></span></p>
    <div class="hero-summary">
      <p>Continuous anomaly detection for sensor telemetry<br>and digital data streams.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="#platform">Explore the platform <svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="product-overview">
  <section class="section container" id="platform" aria-labelledby="platform-title">
    <div class="product-intro">
      <div class="section-label">The platform</div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="platform-title">From raw signal.<br><span class="muted">To informed decision.</span></h2>
        <p>Bring your readings into one workspace. Build monitors around your system, investigate the changes they flag, and test your next design on recorded data.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <dl class="product-stats" aria-label="Available pipeline components">
      <div><dt><span>36</span>Detection models</dt><dd>Statistical, machine-learning and forecast-based detection.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><span>26</span>Signal transforms</dt><dd>Prepare, scale and project the readings that matter.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><span>16</span>Calibration methods</dt><dd>Give anomaly scores a meaningful decision boundary.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <figure class="product-figure">
      <div class="product-screen-frame">
        <div class="product-screen-label mono"><span>Visual composer</span><span>Monitoring workspace</span></div>
        <div class="product-screen-viewport">
<!-- BEGIN PRODUCT COMPOSER -->
<img class="product-screenshot" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Aberration visual composer: pressure, flow and temperature inputs pass through scaling and two parallel detectors into a detection rule and evidence output.">
<!-- END PRODUCT COMPOSER -->
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="product-caption">
        <h3>Build the logic.<br><span class="muted">See every step.</span></h3>
        <div><p>Connect your readings, prepare the inputs and run detectors in parallel. Calibrate their scores, choose a detection rule and keep the evidence. Every step is visible and configurable.</p><p class="product-image-note">Actual visual composer · example cooling-circuit configuration.</p></div>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="section product-band" id="monitoring" aria-labelledby="monitoring-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">Monitoring &amp; reporting</div>
      <div class="product-split product-reporting-intro">
        <div class="product-copy">
          <h2 id="monitoring-title">See the change.<br><span class="muted">Keep the context.</span></h2>
          <p>A flag is the start of an investigation. Follow it back to the readings, inspect the detection evidence and see how the system behaved before and after.</p>
        </div>
        <dl class="product-details">
          <div><dt>Collect the right signals.</dt><dd>Connect MQTT sources, organise their readings and choose what to record. Monitor one signal or a set of related inputs.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>See why it was flagged.</dt><dd>Review readings and detection evidence on a shared timeline. Zoom into a transient, a gradual drift or a change in operating behaviour.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Keep improving the monitor.</dt><dd>Check its operational status, copy recorded readings into the Dojo and test an adjusted design against the same history.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <figure class="product-figure">
        <div class="product-screen-frame">
          <div class="product-screen-label mono"><span>Readings &amp; evidence</span><span>Reporting workspace</span></div>
          <div class="product-screen-viewport">
<!-- BEGIN PRODUCT EVIDENCE -->
<img class="product-screenshot" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Aberration Reporting: an example cooling-circuit pressure reading, flagged events and sequential evidence on a shared timeline.">
<!-- END PRODUCT EVIDENCE -->
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="product-image-note">Actual product interface · illustrative cooling-circuit data, with operating variation, a pressure transient and a developing restriction.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" id="dojo" aria-labelledby="dojo-title">
    <div class="section-label">The Dojo</div>
    <div class="product-split product-dojo">
      <div class="product-copy">
        <h2 id="dojo-title">Try it on the past.<br><span class="muted">Before it watches<br>the present.</span></h2>
        <p>Replay recorded readings or a CSV through a detection pipeline. See what it would have flagged, compare your options, and take a tested design into monitoring.</p>
        {% if docs_base_url | default('') %}<a class="text-link product-docs-link" href="{{ docs_base_url | e }}/user-guide/monitoring/">Explore the workflow <svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17 17 7M7 7h10v10"/></svg></a>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <ol class="product-replay">
        <li><span>Replay</span><div><h3>Give a design some history.</h3><p>Choose recorded data or upload a dataset. Replay it in time order through the same detection logic used in live monitoring.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>Compare</span><div><h3>Find out what it catches.</h3><p>Label known events and compare runs. Look at detected changes, detection delays, and false alarms together.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>Refine</span><div><h3>Take the better design forward.</h3><p>Adjust the pipeline, run it again, and reuse the design in monitoring when you are ready.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="product-loop mono"><span>Recorded data</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Test &amp; compare</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Live monitoring</span><span class="product-loop-note">One workflow. Room to improve.</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-title"><div class="container closing-inner"><div><p class="mono">Connect. Detect. Understand.</p><h2 id="closing-title">Start with a signal.</h2></div><a class="button" href="{{ frontend_base_url | e }}/">Open dashboard <svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17 17 7M7 7h10v10"/></svg></a></div></section>
</div>
</main>  <footer class="site-footer" id="site-footer" tabindex="-1">
  <div class="container footer-main">
    <div class="footer-identity">
      <a class="footer-brand-link" href="#main" aria-label="Aberration home">aberration</a>
      <p>Anomaly detection for <br>connected systems.</p>
    </div>
    <nav class="footer-column" aria-labelledby="footer-product-title">
      <h2 id="footer-product-title">Product</h2>
      <a href="#platform">The platform</a>
      <a href="#monitoring">Monitoring</a>
      <a href="#dojo">The Dojo</a>
      <a href="{{ frontend_base_url | e }}/">Dashboard</a>
    </nav>
    <nav class="footer-column" aria-labelledby="footer-resources-title">
      <h2 id="footer-resources-title">Resources</h2>
      {% if docs_base_url | default('') %}<a href="{{ docs_base_url | e }}/">Documentation</a>
      <a href="{{ docs_base_url | e }}/getting-started/">Getting started</a>{% endif %}
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
      <a href="#security">Report a security issue</a>
    </nav>
    <nav class="footer-column" aria-labelledby="footer-legal-title">
      <h2 id="footer-legal-title">Legal</h2>
      <a href="#impressum">Impressum</a>
      <a href="#privacy">Privacy &amp; cookies</a>
      <a href="#terms">Terms of use</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
  <div class="container footer-bottom">
    <span>© Aberration</span>
    <span class="footer-draft-note">Company details and legal notices are draft placeholders.</span>
    <a href="#main">Back to top ↑</a>
  </div>

  <section class="container legal-panel" id="impressum" aria-labelledby="impressum-heading" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="legal-heading"><h2 id="impressum-heading">Impressum</h2><a class="legal-close" href="#site-footer">Back to footer</a></div>
    <p class="legal-template"><strong>Draft template.</strong> Replace the bracketed fields with verified operator details and remove entries that do not apply.</p>
    <dl class="legal-details">
      <dt>Legal operator</dt><dd>[Full legal name and legal form of the business]</dd>
      <dt>Business address</dt><dd>[Street and number]<br>[Postcode and city]<br>[Country]</dd>
      <dt>Represented by</dt><dd>[Full name(s) of the authorised representative(s), if applicable]</dd>
      <dt>Contact</dt><dd>[Public business email address]<br>[Telephone number or other direct contact channel]</dd>
      <dt>Registration</dt><dd>[Register, registration court and registration number, if applicable]</dd>
      <dt>Business identifiers</dt><dd>[VAT identification number and/or business identification number, if assigned]</dd>
      <dt>Regulated activities</dt><dd>[Supervisory authority, professional body and rules, only if applicable]</dd>
      <dt>Dispute resolution</dt><dd>[Applicable consumer dispute-resolution participation statement and competent body, if required]</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="container legal-panel" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="legal-heading"><h2 id="privacy-heading">Privacy &amp; cookies</h2><a class="legal-close" href="#site-footer">Back to footer</a></div>
    <p class="legal-template"><strong>Draft template.</strong> Complete this notice for the actual website, dashboard, providers and processing practices.</p>
    <dl class="legal-details">
      <dt>Scope &amp; version</dt><dd>[Covered websites and services; date of the latest revision]</dd>
      <dt>Data controller</dt><dd>[Legal name, postal address and privacy contact email]</dd>
      <dt>Data protection contact</dt><dd>[Data protection officer’s contact details, where applicable]</dd>
      <dt>Website visits</dt><dd>[Request/log data, purposes, legal bases and any legitimate interests]</dd>
      <dt>Enquiries &amp; accounts</dt><dd>[Contact and account data; purposes and legal bases; required versus optional information]</dd>
      <dt>Cookies &amp; browser storage</dt><dd>[Names, providers, purposes, lifetimes and consent requirements; distinguish the public site from the signed-in dashboard]</dd>
      <dt>Providers &amp; transfers</dt><dd>[Recipients, hosting and other processors; international transfers and safeguards, if applicable]</dd>
      <dt>Retention</dt><dd>[Retention periods or criteria for each processing purpose]</dd>
      <dt>Your rights</dt><dd>[Applicable access, correction, erasure, restriction, objection, portability and consent-withdrawal rights; how to exercise them]</dd>
      <dt>Complaints</dt><dd>[Relevant supervisory authority and its contact details or website]</dd>
